+# `solution.mpy` construct-to-semantics map
+
+The supplied root `reference-semantics/semantics.k` is an import/assembly file.
+The source terms below are the complete constructor vocabulary used by the
+submitted `solution.mpy`.
+
+| Submitted construct | Declaration | Fixed execution rules | Candidate effect |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| `Module(Stmts)` | `semantics/syntax.k:61` | `core.k:124-127` loads and sequences statements | `#runRescale` embeds this exact module |
+| `ImportFrom("typing","List")` | `syntax.k:43` | `controls.k:35-44`; the non-`math` owise rule is a no-op | none |
+| annotated `FuncDef` | `syntax.k:54`, parameter-list declarations at 57-60 | `functions.k:31-45` creates `closureValC`; `call.k:80-94` enters the frame and allocates cellvars | body is loaded normally |
+| `Params`, `CellVars`, `FreeVars` | `syntax.k:57-60` | `call.k:80-94` and `functions.k:62-75` allocate/bind the parameter and closure cells | none |
+| `Assign(Name(...), Expr)` | `syntax.k:41` with strict RHS | `controls.k:9-18`, `core.k:113-115` write either the local map or a closure cell | both assignments execute; their calls are bridged |
+| `Name` | `syntax.k:12` | `core.k:129-154` walks current, parent, and builtin scopes and dereferences cell-bound names | the `min`/`max` bridges match only after lookup has selected the builtin values |
+| `Call` | `syntax.k:28` | `call.k:18-32`; `core.k:183-191` evaluates callee then arguments left-to-right; `call.k:69-94` handles user frames | priority-40 rules replace the fixed `min` and `max` dispatches on a list value |
+| `Return` | `syntax.k:50` | `functions.k:77-90` records the value, discards the remaining body, restores the caller, and deletes the callee scope | executes normally after the expression bridge |
+| `ListComp` / `CompFor` | `syntax.k:19,35-36` | `comprehension.k:10-26` expands to an accumulator closure and `For`; `controls.k:62-75` iterates; `list.k:12-25` allocates/concatenates | candidate exact-shape bridge replaces the whole expanded computation |
+| `BinOp("-",...)`, `BinOp("/",...)` | `syntax.k:15` with left-to-right `seqstrict(2,3)` | `operators.k:10-13`; `float.k:101-109` maps them to supplied opaque `subF`/`divF`, with concrete LLVM equations | candidate `scaleF` uses the same supplied primitives |
+| `Bool(true)` | `syntax.k:11` | `core.k:193-196`; comprehension guard is generated by `comprehension.k:24-26` | exact bridge requires this literal |
+| list iteration/value | `core.k:14,18,25-40` | `list.k:8-15` supplies iteration and literal allocation | synthetic harness passes an unboxed `list(VS)` value; ordinary `ListExpr` arguments are heap references |
+
+Configuration and state footprint:
+
+- `core.k:49-60` declares `<k>`, `<env>`, `<scopes>`, `<scopeLoc>`,
+  `<heap>`, `<heapLoc>`, `<stack>`, `<ret>`, `<exc>`, and `<exit-code>`.
+- Fixed execution of the direct-list `[1.0,2.0]` witness ends at
+  `<heapLoc> 7` after two closure cells, the empty accumulator, two singleton
+  lists, and two concatenation results.
+- Candidate bridge execution of the same synthetic entry ends at
+  `<heapLoc> 3`: two closure cells plus only the final list allocation.
+- The candidate claim existentially frames final scope and heap state, so this
+  state mismatch is hidden from its postcondition.
